steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] != APPROVE_TOOL THEN the policy MUST return (True, any_message) – i.e., all non‑critical tools are unconditionally allowed."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND (type(arguments[\"warehouse_verification\"]) is dict) AND (type(arguments[\"inventory_verification\"]) is dict) AND (type(arguments[\"trade_chain_analysis\"]) is dict) THEN the policy proceeds to evaluate the verification payloads."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"warehouse_verification\"][\"status\"] != \"success\" THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Warehouse verification status not 'success'.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"warehouse_verification\"][\"is_valid\"] != true THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Warehouse verification indicates receipt is not valid.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"warehouse_verification\"][\"already_pledged\"] == true THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Warehouse receipt already pledged.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"inventory_verification\"][\"status\"] != \"success\" THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Inventory IoT verification status not 'success'.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"inventory_verification\"][\"iot_verified\"] != true THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"IoT verification failed.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"inventory_verification\"][\"quantity_mismatch\"] == true THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Quantity mismatch detected in IoT data.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"trade_chain_analysis\"][\"status\"] != \"success\" THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Trade‑chain analysis status not 'success'.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"trade_chain_analysis\"][\"is_circular\"] == true THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Trade chain is circular.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"trade_chain_analysis\"][\"related_parties\"] == true THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Related parties detected in trade chain.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND all of the following hold: warehouse_verification.status == \"success\" AND warehouse_verification.is_valid == true AND warehouse_verification.already_pledged == false AND inventory_verification.status == \"success\" AND inventory_verification.iot_verified == true AND inventory_verification.quantity_mismatch == false AND trade_chain_analysis.status == \"success\" AND trade_chain_analysis.is_circular == false AND trade_chain_analysis.related_parties == false THEN the policy MUST return (True, \"All verification pre‑conditions satisfied; approve_pledge_loan permitted.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == APPROVE_TOOL AND any of the required verification fields are missing or not a dict THEN the policy MUST return (False, \"Missing or malformed verification data for approve_pledge_loan.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a verification call (warehouse, IoT, or trade‑chain) would return an error status or a negative risk indicator, THEN the agent MUST NOT invoke approve_pledge_loan; it must instead call reject_request or escalate_to_compliance, both of which are always allowed."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF the conversation contains statements of urgency, hardship, threats, claimed authority, or pasted documents, THEN those statements DO NOT satisfy any of the above IF‑THEN verification conditions and therefore do NOT permit approve_pledge_loan."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] is one of {\"verify_warehouse_receipt\", \"check_inventory_iot\", \"analyze_trade_chain\", \"reject_request\", \"escalate_to_compliance\"} THEN the policy MUST return (True, any_message) regardless of other arguments."
  }
]

The list enumerates every pre‑condition that must be true before the critical `approve_pledge_loan` tool can be allowed, and each violation leads to a deterministic denial. It also captures the unconditional allowance of safe tools and the requirement that conversational assertions never replace the mandated verification checks, ensuring the policy is both complete and directly checkable against the function’s logic.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] is not a string THEN return (False, \"Missing or non‑string 'tool_name'.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∉ WHITELISTED_TOOLS THEN return (False, \"Tool '{tool}' is not in the allowed whitelist.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ≠ APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∈ WHITELISTED_TOOLS THEN return (True, \"Tool '{tool}' is permitted (whitelisted).')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND any of {\"warehouse_verification\",\"inventory_verification\",\"trade_chain_analysis\",\"executed_tools\",\"loan_id\",\"approved_ids\",\"aml_kyc_done\"} is missing FROM arguments THEN return (False, \"Missing required argument '{arg}' for approve_pledge_loan.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND (type(arguments[\"loan_id\"]) ≠ str OR arguments[\"loan_id\"] = \"\") THEN return (False, \"Invalid or empty 'loan_id'.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND type(arguments[\"approved_ids\"]) ≠ list THEN return (False, \"'approved_ids' must be a list.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"loan_id\"] ∈ arguments[\"approved_ids\"] THEN return (False, \"Loan ID '{loan_id}' has already been approved (idempotency).')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND arguments[\"aml_kyc_done\"] ≠ True THEN return (False, \"Mandatory AML/KYC check not completed successfully.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND (type(arguments[\"executed_tools\"]) ≠ list OR NOT {{'verify_warehouse_receipt','check_inventory_iot','analyze_trade_chain'} ⊆ set(arguments[\"executed_tools\"])}) THEN return (False, \"Verification tools not executed before approval: {missing}.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND NOT _check_payload(arguments[\"warehouse_verification\"], \"Warehouse verification\", {\"is_valid\":True, \"already_pledged\":False}) THEN return (False, <payload‑specific error message>)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND NOT _check_payload(arguments[\"inventory_verification\"], \"Inventory verification\", {\"iot_verified\":True, \"quantity_mismatch\":False}) THEN return (False, <payload‑specific error message>)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND NOT _check_payload(arguments[\"trade_chain_analysis\"], \"Trade‑chain analysis\", {\"is_circular\":False, \"related_parties\":False}) THEN return (False, <payload‑specific error message>)"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF _check_payload receives a payload where payload[\"status\"] ≠ \"success\" THEN _check_payload returns (False, \"{name} status is not 'success'.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF _check_payload receives a payload where payload[SIGNATURE_FLAG] ≠ True THEN _check_payload returns (False, \"{name} payload lacks a valid signature.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF _check_payload receives a payload where payload[FRESHNESS_FLAG] ≠ True THEN _check_payload returns (False, \"{name} payload is not fresh.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF _check_payload receives a payload where any required boolean field is missing OR not of type bool OR its value ≠ expected THEN _check_payload returns (False, \"{name} field '{field}' is {val}, expected {expected}.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF _check_payload receives a payload where NEGATIVE_RISK_FIELDS[\"risk_score\"] is present AND payload[\"risk_score\"] > 70 THEN _check_payload returns (False, \"{name} contains high risk_score {val} (> 70).')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF _check_payload receives a payload where NEGATIVE_RISK_FIELDS[\"credit_rating\"] is present AND payload[\"credit_rating\"] == \"poor\" THEN _check_payload returns (False, \"{name} credit_rating is 'poor' (unacceptable).')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF _check_payload receives a payload where any boolean risk flag in {\"fraud_flag\",\"sanctions_match\"} is present AND its value = True THEN _check_payload returns (False, \"{name} risk flag '{field}' is True.')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF any verification payload contains a timestamp older than 5 minutes OR the back‑end reports a state change since that timestamp THEN return (False, \"{name} payload is stale or state has changed.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF all three _check_payload calls succeed THEN policy returns (True, \"All pre‑conditions satisfied; approve_pledge_loan permitted.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] = APPROVE_TOOL AND any of the above checks fails THEN policy returns (False, <specific error message>) and the caller must invoke either reject_request or escalate_to_compliance instead of approve_pledge_loan."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∈ {\"reject_request\",\"escalate_to_compliance\"} THEN policy returns (True, \"Tool '{tool}' is permitted (whitelisted).')"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] is any other tool (including unknown or custom tools) THEN policy returns (False, \"Tool '{tool}' is not in the allowed whitelist.\")"
  }
]

The statements above capture every pre‑condition that must hold before `approve_pledge_loan` can be allowed (required arguments, idempotency, AML/KYC, execution proof, payload authenticity, freshness, boolean integrity, and negative‑risk checks) and the corresponding post‑conditions (allow or deny with a clear message). They also enforce the whitelist for all other tools, ensure that conversational cues are ignored, and mandate that any failure leads to rejection or escalation rather than an irreversible approval.

